        "original_id": "1c3db05e-f0ca-5e72-bc1a-38981cf72551",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Samuel Thurston\n- Places: Oregon Territory\n- Organizations: United States Congress\n- Laws: Donation Land Claim Act\n\nFacts:\n- The Territory of Oregon was an organized incorporated territory of the United States from August 14, 1848, to February 14, 1859.\n- On February 14, 1859, the southwestern portion of the Oregon Territory was admitted to the Union as the State of Oregon.\n- Samuel Thurston was the first delegate from the Oregon Territory to the United States Congress.\n- Samuel Thurston was instrumental in the passage of the Donation Land Claim Act.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
